{"body":{"text":["A component is a holon, and says in it only what it says, its `input`, and its body where it is data. The code that realizes it on the web is the web's components' own, in `components/web/`, which give the web's chassis, in `chassis/web/`, the map of it, found by the component's id and never its name (`components/web/realized.ts`); components realized on another surface keep a map of their own. The chassis names no component: whoever starts it gives it the components, what each is called, and the ones it draws for its own cases, the one that chooses where several could draw a value, the fallback, and Problem, as OpenLight's chassis mounted components of its own (21/39); it stands apart from the components it draws, since a local chassis will come beside the web's: \"we know we're going to want local chassis anyway\" (20/19). *The chassis broken away, the author's, 20/17 and 20/19; where the code lies the session's (20/18); built.* Some components, as the reader and search, are defined wholly in the field, as layout and data (15/19). *Components as holons, settled 2026-11-11.* A component declares its `input` as a function does, a list of types matched by type (18/27), and is applied by a use, which names it and gives it what it is to show; mount folds into use, \"I'm fine with the dropping mount until we feel the need of it again\" (18/71). *Settled, 18/93; built.*"]},"id":"1M86HM1CY87M000","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A component is a function of what it is given and of the field, and keeps no state: \"The UI was always supposed to be stateless\" (21/63). It is given `io`, the chassis's actions where it is drawn, named from the author's own word for programs, \"it's I/O\" (16/5, 21/49, 21/51): `read`, the field as it renders, the value, or nothing until it answers; `ask`, the field once, as a handler does; `draw`, a value within it, by whatever draws that; `propose`, a value back through the way back, committed; `remove`, it taken out of the list it stands in; and `pick`, where a component is to be chosen. \"If I invoke a read, of course the chassis will be aware of me invoking a read. … And when it comes in, it's just a value. Why can't I use that value directly?\" (21/57). No helper stands between, nor signals; the TSX is plain markup (21/55). *The author's, 21/57 and 21/63; `io` his, 21/51; built.*"]},"id":"1M86HM1CY87M001","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A component reads by an expression of the language written in its code as a template, ``q`print(${step})` ``: \"let's use template literals for now\" (21/47). The language reads the template's text as a lambda over its holes, once for each template, and the chassis applies that lambda to what is put into them, each quoted, so a value is never read as words. Its functions are named by their bare names, which a function of the same name in any store mounted would make ambiguous; naming them by route was weighed, and left as the path Templates naming functions by route. A builder of uses in TypeScript, calls as uses and lambdas traced, was weighed and set aside (21/45). An editor on the field, the author holds, will change all of it: \"once we get there, everything's going to be different anyway\" (21/47). *Templates the author's, 21/47; how they are read the session's; built.*"]},"id":"1M86HM1CY87M002","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The chassis does for every component what each would else do for itself, reads being what a framework calls its state: \"reads are the \\\"state management\\\" of the \\\"framework\\\"\" (21/31). It asks the reads of one turn of every component as one read of the engine, kept live, each told its own part of the answer, and each asked alone again where that one read fails; renders a component again when what it is given changes, or an answer says something new, and lays the new render over the page, changing only what differs, so focus, a caret and a scroll stay (21/59, 21/61); keeps each drawing in place by its key, a holon by its id, a drawing by the uses it was reached through; shows a drawing made anew, or a render waiting on its reads, once every read within it has answered, so nothing shows piece by piece, or after two seconds; and stands each drawing as a boundary, the component Problem drawn in its place, given what failed, where what it is given, a read it asks or its render fails (21/39). Where the way back finds no change, the chassis marks the place fixed, a fact of the place no render undoes. It draws nothing a person sees beyond a host for each drawing: the inspector and the bar showing the page busy are the page's (21/33). A component holding what the browser keeps for it, as the input does with what is typed and what completion offers, gives its node with how to update it, and is updated in place of rendering. *The chassis's work the session's, at the author's word (21/25, 21/31, 21/35, 21/71); built, 271 tests passing.*"]},"id":"1M86HM1CY87M003","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A component's look is the chassis's too, and shipped with the components, not with the site: \"the components look probably should be shipped with them. That's the component's responsibility\" (19/15). Styling has its degree, the author said, while what looks wholly different may want other components; so the look's variables are opened, to be tuned, by a knob component perhaps, and later taken from the field (19/15). On the web it stands in `components/web/look/`, a stylesheet a component, beneath them the page's ground and the tokens; one built stylesheet and the faces are what a site links, and beside it the chassis's own, in `chassis/web/look/`, and the inspector's, the page's, in `site/`. The material, a stylesheet kept as text in glass that nothing read, was let go with its type: \"I don't see the point of the material\" (19/13, 19/15). *The look shipped with the components, its variables opened and the material let go, the author's, 19/15; its layout the session's; built.*"]},"id":"1M86HM1CY87M004","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The chassis's look holds its tokens, which every component draws with and a site tunes, and what the chassis makes itself, a drawing's host and a line where even Problem could not draw, in `chassis/web/look/`. A link is made in one place, `chassis/web/href.ts`, as the page keeps its address, and no component reads the address: an answer says what was asked by its steps, as the pills say them, and a list keeps how it was shown by what it holds. The breadcrumb is one read of `wholes` and the start one of `roots`, functions written in the language. *The session's, at the author's word to clean what it could before he reviews (20/21); built.*"]},"id":"1M86HM1CY87M005","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["What a use naming no component gives is drawn by the component that takes it, found by `taking`, a function of the language, not the chassis's: of the functions or components it is given to choose among, those that take all that is given, as a use giving it would be judged, some placeholder taking something given of a type of the field it takes. So a brief draws as a brief, and a list with the direction it runs as a list. Whether a function or a component takes what is given is the native `takes`, giving what each placeholder takes, or null: native because how a use's args meet an input is the evaluator's own, so the rule is written once and the chassis rebuilds nothing of the engine. The author asked for finding as one simple expression: \"It should just be one simple expression, right?\" (20/25), matching every argument: \"we match against multiple arguments, not only one\" (20/27). A component over a kind of value alone, a list or a string, is never found so, since many take one shape for different ends, and is drawn only where a use names it; what nothing takes by a type is drawn by the fallback the chassis is given, Value, showing any holon as its values, so nothing is left unshown, and what holds no holon is given it at once, nothing read. One found draws it and is found again each time, nothing written into the field as the chassis draws (21/25); where several fit, a chooser lists them and the person's pick is drawn for the page, never guessed. How a component is to be chosen, as chrome given the chassis or in the context menu, the author has not settled: \"in this I'm sceptical of the chassis doing anything UI related\" (21/33), taking hardwired meanwhile (21/35). *Open: the path Choosing a component as chrome.* *Finding as one expression over every argument, the author's (20/25, 20/27); takes and taking the session's (20/28); the name `taking` the session's, taken by the author (20/32, 20/33); built.*"]},"id":"1M86HM1CY87M006","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Its commits are judged, minted and landed in strata, tested with stores that fail, refuse or answer changed every time, with many changes, and with two engines over one storage at once. The page at `/`, the command line and the author's tools all read and commit through it, and 271 tests pass. Before the earlier engine went, the new one was held to it question by question over every store: 60 the same, 11 refused by design, and 6 apart from the migration itself. It runs on Bun 1.4.4, since Bun 1.3.11 lost a message now and then on MessagePorts between workers."]},"id":"1M86HM1CY87M007","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Since components render on the chassis, a move takes about 70 to 210 ms in the browser, where it took 45 to 150. Timed step by step (21/84): the query committed, the root read again while the reads of the page before ran again, a component found by type in 20 to 33 ms, then reads waiting on the reads before them, the 79 functions about 50 ms of it. Every kept read is worked out again, whole, whenever a store it stood on moves, and every read stands on every store; component renders are already only where something changed, the waste the engine's (21/88). A store telling, with its head, what its commits touched, and a kept read running again only where it read one, was built and reverted for losing changes silently (21/93); a kept read checking again, by content, the holons it used was weighed and held, its gain too small for a second path in the engine: \"if it is simple and provides strong benefit it makes sense\" (21/94). Re-deriving only where a change flows, the author holds, is \"a requirement of an engine\" (21/90), the bigger step its successor (21/96). *Open: the thread Reads re-derived where a change flows.*"]},"id":"1M86HM1CY87M008","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["**The author's review of the components and the chassis,** which the next session takes (21/98), the components now plain functions of what they are given and the field, read through `io` (21/57)."]},"id":"1M86HM1CY87M009","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**The old wiki's fate:** whether The wiki, kept as it stood, is let go, as the author leaned to if Knowledge holds all it does (18/105), and whether the reasoning it alone holds comes into Knowledge first. *Open, awaiting the author.*"]},"id":"1M86HM1CY87M00A","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**Fewer passes to the stores:** \"I would thikn it shouldn t need many passes to the store if we have the right native vocabulary\" (19/72). A brief is now read in one read, and what a read applies learned a layer at a time, each function it names asked whole (20/16, 20/34); it is still learned every read, and knowing it across reads would be the engine keeping something, a deeper discussion the author set apart: \"architecturally, that's not what we drew\" (20/11). The reads of a page run again on each move of the query, and re-deriving only where a change flows is the engine's successor (21/90, 21/96). *Open; the thread Reads re-derived where a change flows.*"]},"id":"1M86HM1CY87M00B","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**The git integration:** the linked code of holons seen, the repository's tree navigable as it is, one store on the start page (19/19); read-only first, as the session proposed."]},"id":"1M86HM1CY87M00C","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**Reading git from a browser, tested:** a repository served as plain files read from a page, with no proxy and no limit, before building on it (19/24)."]},"id":"1M86HM1CY87M00D","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**The stores read through git,** locally and published alike, the build no longer copying them (19/21)."]},"id":"1M86HM1CY87M00E","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**Then the threads** standing open, divergence first among them: when a commit lands in some stores it touches and misses others, the holons it wrote marked diverged, the later commit's version found to answer, and the share not delivered kept while the engine lives, as settled at 12/77. *Open: where the mark is kept, and so whether a read may then ask for a holon only where holding says it lies; the threads Where divergence is marked, Where a holon is kept and Holding links to history.*"]},"id":"1M86HM1CY87M00F","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**The command line able to commit,** so the field is written through the engine by hand and the author's tools in `author/` go. *The tools going, settled 2026-11-11.*"]},"id":"1M86HM1CY87M00G","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**Holons read as the type asked,** as the buffer of characters is read as a string."]},"id":"1M86HM1CY87M00H","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["*The engine, the interface and the stores were merged onto main and the site published (19/25); the expressions as uses, the buffer, the interface and the site on the engine, the stores in strata and components declared in their holons, the steps before these, are built, as each part says. The chassis was broken away at the author's word (20/19), and the components made plain functions over `io`, rendered and laid out by it (21/57, 21/71), built; the git integration is next (19/19). The order is the session's. Proposed.*"]},"id":"1M86HM1CY87M00J","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
