{"body":{"text":["The page hosts and decides little: it starts the engine and each store in a worker of its own, mounts the stores, and draws its root read, Reader given the query's text, turning the address, back and forward, into what it draws. Which components show, and how they are laid out, are read from the field. It is `site/page.ts`, served at `/`, and puts the chassis and the components together; the language as glass ships it, its types and the functions everything applies found by route, is `language/shipped.ts`, and the interface is no module of the code but this program, the page running a chassis with its components on the engine (20/18). What the chassis draws nothing of is the page's: the inspector, on right-click, `site/inspector.tsx`, and the bar showing the page busy while the chassis waits on reads, `site/busy.ts`."]},"id":"1M86HM1CY87M01H","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}